  "latest": {
    "version": "0.20.2",
    "notes": "Ancilla v0.20.2 \u2014 Deep research. Agents in view.\n\nAn open-source desktop and web workspace for Muse Code by AMAZONIA WORKS, available on Windows, macOS and Linux.\n\n**Deep Research:** investigate questions with parallel workers, follow their searches and sources, and save cited reports as PDF, Word or HTML. **Crew:** follow ordinary prompts and tools alongside workflows, native agents and background tasks, with timelines, live status and controls for work that needs you.\n\n**New in 0.20.2**\n- Guided **Sign in with Meta** from Home and Settings, with browser instructions, a copyable code, confirmation, retry and cancellation.\n- **Save As** for PDF, Word and HTML research reports on desktop and supported browsers.\n- Crew now tracks the lead and foreground tools during ordinary prompts, keeps completed work inspectable, and follows workers that outlive the lead.\n- Plans follow their actual turn and workers, preserve unfinished steps, and retain completed checklists.\n- Compact completion summaries, clearer tool inspectors, faster history handling, and reliable login cancellation and retry.\n\nRead [what changed in this release](https://github.com/aleff-ferreira/ancilla/blob/v0.20.2/docs/CHANGELOG.md) or [explore the interface](https://github.com/aleff-ferreira/ancilla/blob/v0.20.2/README.md).\n\n**What you need.** Ancilla bundles Node.js. Install Meta's Muse Code CLI, then choose **Sign in with Meta** in Ancilla and approve access using the account that owns your Muse Code plan. An existing Muse login is reused. Windows supports native Muse or Muse inside WSL2; setup shows the instructions for your selected runtime.\n\n**Which file.** Windows: the `x64-setup.exe` installer. macOS, Apple Silicon and Intel alike: the `universal.dmg`. Linux: the `amd64.AppImage`; mark it executable, then run it. From then on Ancilla updates itself from these releases, and refuses any update that is not signed with its key.\n\n**Unsigned installers.** The Windows installer is not Authenticode-signed yet, so SmartScreen may warn about an unrecognised app: choose More info, then Run anyway. The macOS app is not notarized by Apple yet, so its first launch needs a right-click on the app, then Open.\n\n**Licenses.** Ancilla is free software under the [GNU AGPL v3](https://github.com/aleff-ferreira/ancilla/blob/v0.20.2/LICENSE). Portions derive from Helicon, Copyright (c) 2026 Harjot Singh Rana and contributors, under the MIT License; its notice is kept in [LICENSE-HELICON](https://github.com/aleff-ferreira/ancilla/blob/v0.20.2/LICENSE-HELICON). The third-party software each build bundles, Node.js among it, is listed with its licenses in [THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md](https://github.com/aleff-ferreira/ancilla/blob/v0.20.2/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md), which also ships inside the app.",
